 "defect_observations": [
  "Table EPR row (first-order-depth.tex 284-286, 291-292) says the cited complexity convention omits identity and that logical equality is not included in the row's theorem, while thm:p02-w02-p02-035-bsr-complexity (body 452-459) proves NEXPTIME-completeness with or without equality; the row understates the proved scope (consistency, not coverage).",
  "Lewis1980, cited for the monadic and EPR rows (first-order-depth.tex 229, 288), is not in held-sources.json, so its locators cannot be checked; the row claims are independently proved in the owned body/annex from held BorgerGradelGurevich1997 and GradelKolaitisVardi1997.",
  "The GF finite-model property (body 650-654, annex 790-862) and all NEXPTIME/2EXPTIME/EXPTIME lower bounds rest on declared imported premises: def:p02-w02-p02-035-herwig-import (body 636-648), def:p02-w02-p02-035-domino-import (body 65-85; its source leaves the vertical relation of BGG thm. 6.1.2 as an exercise), def:p02-w02-p02-035-alternation-import (body 734-749). The theorem environments carry proved= tags without restating the premise in the statement; the dependency is declared in the adjacent proofboundary environments and prose (e.g. body 93-97). The decision procedures themselves (type elimination, grounding, colour sets, Scott guess-and-check) do not depend on these imports.",
  "Body 846-851 asserts the printed source sentence of Gradel1999 thm. 4.4 has no model; a source-fidelity claim not reviewed here."
